# Frontend Performance Skill

When doing frontend-related work (UI, React/Vue components, pages, layouts, CSS, forms, tables, dashboards, routes, or client performance/UX), you MUST:

1. Read and follow the `frontend-performance` skill at:
   `C:\Users\BRANDON\.cursor\skills\frontend-performance\SKILL.md`
2. Apply its objectives as relevant to the current task (no full-page reloads, skeleton loaders, optimistic UI, undo patterns, caching, real-time over polling, standardized UI states, and performance audits).
3. Prefer incremental, scoped changes that match the existing design system unless the user asks for a broader refactor.
